# The build context is backend/ (see render.yaml dockerContext). Render builds
# from a fresh clone where most of these do not exist, so nothing here changes
# what ships today — it changes what a *local* `docker build` produces, which
# until now was not the same image. `COPY . .` runs after `uv sync`, so a host
# .venv lands on top of the image's own, and the host one's python is a symlink
# into /opt/homebrew that does not exist in the container.
#
# The rest is the same idea: a dev database, a real .env and a stale
# staticfiles/ are all things that would otherwise be baked into an image and
# shipped.
.venv/
db*.sqlite3
.env*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
staticfiles/
.DS_Store
